/**
 * @defgroup StSsdSimulationMaker StSsdSimulationMaker — SSD Slow / Full Simulation
 *
 * @brief Full-chain slow simulation for the STAR Silicon Strip Detector (SSD, layer 7).
 *
 * @details
 * ## Overview
 *
 * The SSD slow simulation converts primary GEANT energy-deposition records into
 * digitised strip signals that are indistinguishable in format from real detector
 * readout.  The chain comprises three consecutive STAR Makers:
 *
 * | Step | Maker             | Input table      | Output table     |
 * |------|-------------------|------------------|------------------|
 * | 1    | St_sls_Maker      | g2t_ssd_hit      | sls_strip        |
 * | 2    | St_spa_Maker      | sls_strip        | spa_strip        |
 * | 3    | StSsdEmbeddingMaker | spa_strip (simu) + spa_strip (real) | spa_strip (merged) |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Detector Geometry
 *
 * The SSD occupies layer 7 of the STAR SVT/SSD system and consists of 20 ladders,
 * each carrying several double-sided silicon strip detector (DSSD) wafers.  Every
 * wafer has two strip planes:
 *
 * - **P-side** (junction side): strips parallel to the short axis.
 * - **N-side** (ohmic side): strips inclined by the stereo angle @f$\theta@f$
 *   with respect to the P-side, enabling 2D hit reconstruction from the
 *   intersection of fired-strip pairs on the two sides.
 *
 * A unique wafer identifier is packed as:
 * @f[
 *   \text{idWafer} = \text{layer} \times 1000 + \text{wafer} \times 100 + \text{ladder}
 * @f]
 * and a strip identifier as:
 * @f[
 *   \text{id\_strip} = 10000 \times (10 \times n_\text{strip} + \text{side}) + \text{idWafer}
 * @f]
 * where @f$\text{side} = 0@f$ for the P-side and @f$\text{side} = 1@f$ for the N-side.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Physics of Charge Deposition (Step 1 — St_sls_Maker)
 *
 * ### Energy loss
 * GEANT propagates each primary or secondary track through the 300 μm thick
 * silicon bulk.  The deposited energy @f$\Delta E@f$ follows a Landau
 * distribution.  For a minimum-ionising particle (MIP):
 * @f[
 *   \langle \Delta E \rangle \approx 100\;\text{keV/cm} \times 300\;\mu\text{m}
 *                           \approx 30\;\text{keV}
 * @f]
 *
 * ### Electron–hole pair creation
 * The deposited energy is converted to a number of electron–hole (e–h) pairs
 * using the mean pair-creation energy @f$\epsilon@f$
 * (parameter `slsCtrl_st::pairCreationEnergy`, typically 3.62 eV for silicon at
 * room temperature):
 * @f[
 *   N_{e\!-\!h} = \frac{\Delta E}{\epsilon}
 * @f]
 *
 * ### Charge diffusion
 * Carriers drift to the collecting strips under the bias field.  Transverse
 * diffusion broadens the charge cloud.  The r.m.s. spread @f$\sigma@f$ on the
 * P-side and N-side is parameterised by `parDiffP` and `parDiffN` respectively
 * (extracted from beam-test measurements).  The fraction of the total charge
 * collected on the @f$k@f$-th strip is:
 * @f[
 *   f_k = \frac{1}{2}\left[
 *           \mathrm{erf}\!\left(\frac{x_{k+1/2}}{\sqrt{2}\,\sigma}\right) -
 *           \mathrm{erf}\!\left(\frac{x_{k-1/2}}{\sqrt{2}\,\sigma}\right)
 *         \right]
 * @f]
 * where @f$x_{k\pm 1/2}@f$ are the boundaries of strip @f$k@f$ relative to the
 * hit position.
 *
 * ### Capacitive induction
 * Adjacent strips pick up an induced charge through inter-strip capacitance.
 * Right- and left-neighbour induction amplitudes are controlled by
 * `parIndRightP`, `parIndLeftP` (P-side) and `parIndRightN`, `parIndLeftN`
 * (N-side), also from beam-test fits.
 *
 * ### Ideal → Real geometry translation
 * GEANT computes hit positions in an idealised geometry.  The
 * `ideal2RealTranslation()` method corrects for mechanical mis-alignment by
 * propagating the track helix (StPhysicalHelixD) — constructed from the
 * GEANT-level momentum and charge — onto the real wafer plane defined by its
 * centre position and normal vector read from the `ssdWafersPosition` database
 * table.  If the intersection falls outside the active area of the nominal wafer,
 * the search is extended to the neighbouring ladders (±1).
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Electronics and DAQ Simulation (Step 2 — St_spa_Maker)
 *
 * Each of the 491 520 strips (20 ladders × wafers/ladder × 2 × 768 strips/side)
 * receives a Gaussian noise contribution sampled from the per-strip noise and
 * pedestal values stored in the `ssdStripCalib` calibration database table:
 * @f[
 *   Q_\text{out} = Q_\text{signal} + \mathcal{N}(0,\,\sigma_\text{strip})
 * @f]
 * A pedestal subtraction is then applied, followed by a DAQ zero-suppression
 * threshold cut.  Only strips whose signal exceeds the cut are written to the
 * `spa_strip` output table.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Embedding (Step 3 — StSsdEmbeddingMaker)
 *
 * For embedding studies (simulated tracks embedded in real collisions) the maker
 * merges the simulated `spa_strip` table with the real-data `spa_strip` table
 * decoded from the DAQ stream.  For strips fired in both samples the ADC counts
 * are summed:
 * @f[
 *   \text{ADC}_\text{merged} = \text{ADC}_\text{simu} + \text{ADC}_\text{real}
 * @f]
 * Strips present in only one sample are copied to the output unchanged.  MC truth
 * information (`id_mchit`, `id_mctrack`) from the simulated strips is preserved.
 *
 * The maker can operate in three modes:
 * - **Embedding** (default): merge simu + real.
 * - **Plain simulation**: run with simulated strips only (no real data).
 * - **Skip**: if `mDoEmbedding` is set but no SSD data exist in the DAQ stream and
 *   `mPlainSimIfNoSSD` is false, the event is discarded.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Data-flow diagram
 * @verbatim
 *  GEANT (g2t_ssd_hit / g2t_svt_hit)
 *        |
 *        v
 *  St_sls_Maker::readPointFromTableWithEmbedding()
 *    - ideal→real geometry correction (StPhysicalHelixD)
 *    - fills StSsdBarrel hit collections
 *        |
 *  St_sls_Maker::chargeSharingOverStrip()
 *    - e-h pair creation, diffusion, induction
 *    - fills StSsdStrip signal lists
 *        |
 *  St_sls_Maker::writeStripToTable()   --> sls_strip table
 *        |
 *  St_spa_Maker::Make()
 *    - readStripFromTable(sls_strip)
 *    - readNoiseFromTable(ssdStripCalib)
 *    - addNoiseToStrip()
 *    - doDaqSimulation()              --> spa_strip table
 *        |
 *  StSsdEmbeddingMaker::AddRawData()
 *    - merge spa_strip(simu) + spa_strip(real)
 *                                     --> spa_strip (merged) table
 * @endverbatim
 *
 * @authors B. Hippolyte, W. Pinganaud (original, 2000);
 *          J. Bouchet (embedding maker, 2008)
 *
 * @see http://star.in2p3.fr/STAR_informatique/simulators.html#sls
 */


