 */


// ============================================================
// Class: St_sls_Maker
// ============================================================

/**
 * @class St_sls_Maker
 * @ingroup StSsdSimulationMaker
 * @brief Strip Lazy Simulator — converts GEANT hits to SSD strip signals.
 *
 * @details
 * St_sls_Maker is the first stage of the SSD slow simulation.  It reads
 * GEANT hit records from the @c g2t_ssd_hit (or legacy @c g2t_svt_hit) table,
 * corrects the hit position from the idealised GEANT geometry to the real
 * (survey-corrected) detector geometry using helix tracking, computes the
 * electron–hole charge deposited on each strip through diffusion and capacitive
 * induction, and writes the resulting analogue strip signals to the @c sls_strip
 * table.
 *
 * All physics parameters (pair-creation energy, diffusion coefficients,
 * induction amplitudes) are read at the start of each run from the @c slsCtrl
 * database table via StSsdDbMaker.
 *
 * ### Data member summary
 *
 * | Member               | Type                    | Description                                     |
 * |----------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|
 * | `m_ctrl`             | `slsCtrl_st *`          | Control/physics parameters (not owned)          |
 * | `m_dimensions`       | `St_ssdDimensions *`    | Detector geometry table (not owned)             |
 * | `m_positions`        | `St_ssdWafersPosition *`| Per-wafer survey positions (not owned)          |
 * | `mBField`            | `double`                | @f$B_z@f$ at the origin [T·kilogauss unit]      |
 * | `mHit`               | `StMcSsdHit *`          | Transient MC hit object                         |
 * | `mSsdLayer`          | `Int_t`                 | SSD layer number (always 7)                     |
 * | `mNLadder`           | `Int_t`                 | Number of ladders (20)                          |
 * | `mNWaferPerLadder`   | `Int_t`                 | Number of wafers per ladder (from DB)           |
 * | `mNStripPerSide`     | `Int_t`                 | Number of strips per side per wafer (from DB)   |
 * | `mActiveLadders[20]` | `Int_t[20]`             | Active ladder mask (reserved)                   |
 * | `mDetectorLargeEdge` | `Float_t`               | Full active length along beam [cm]              |
 * | `mDetectorSmallEdge` | `Float_t`               | Full active width (transverse) [cm]             |
 * | `mStripPitch`        | `Float_t`               | Strip pitch [cm]                                |
 * | `mTheta`             | `Float_t`               | Stereo angle between P- and N-side strips [rad] |
 * | `counter`            | `Int_t *`               | Per-wafer hit counter (diagnostic)              |
 * | `hRejected`          | `TH1F *`                | Histogram: fraction of hits surviving dead-zone removal |
 * | `mDimensions`        | `ssdDimensions_st *`    | Cached pointer to raw geometry struct           |
 * | `mcEvent`            | `StMcEvent *` (prot.)   | Pointer to the MC event (filled per event)      |
 * | `N`                  | `Int_t` (prot.)         | Number of rows in the wafer-position table      |
 * | `positions`          | `ssdWafersPosition_st *`(prot.) | Raw pointer to wafer-position array    |
 *
 * @authors B. Hippolyte, W. Pinganaud
 * @date 2000
 */

/**
 * @fn St_sls_Maker::St_sls_Maker(const char *name)
 * @brief Constructor.
 * @details Initialises @c mHit and @c m_ctrl to @c nullptr.
 * @param name Maker name passed to StMaker base class; default is @c "sls_strip".
 */

/**
 * @fn St_sls_Maker::~St_sls_Maker()
 * @brief Destructor. No heap memory is owned by this class.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::Init()
 * @brief One-time initialisation.
 * @details If the @c ".histos" attribute is set, allocates the @c hRejected
 *          diagnostic histogram.
 * @return @c kStOk always.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::InitRun(Int_t runNumber)
 * @brief Per-run initialisation.
 * @details Retrieves the @c slsCtrl, @c ssdDimensions, and @c ssdWafersPosition
 *          tables from StSsdDbMaker.  Reads the magnetic field z-component from
 *          StarMagField at the origin and stores it in @c mBField.
 * @param runNumber STAR run number (used by the base class to route DB queries).
 * @return @c kStOk on success; @c kStFatal if any required database table is absent.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::Make()
 * @brief Per-event processing — full hit-to-strip conversion.
 * @details
 * Execution sequence:
 * -# Fetch geometry parameters and call setSsdParameters().
 * -# Create the output @c sls_strip table (capacity 40 000 rows).
 * -# Retrieve @c g2t_ssd_hit (preferred) or fall back to @c g2t_svt_hit.
 * -# Call readPointFromTableWithEmbedding() to load hits into StSsdBarrel and
 *    apply ideal→real geometry correction.
 * -# Call convertGlobalFrameToOther() on the barrel.
 * -# Call removeInactiveHitInTable() to purge hits in dead zones.
 * -# Call chargeSharingOverStrip() to compute strip signals.
 * -# Call writeStripToTable() to serialise signals into @c sls_strip.
 * -# Reset the barrel for the next event.
 * @return @c kStOK if at least one strip was produced; @c kStWarn otherwise.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::Finish()
 * @brief End-of-job clean-up. Currently a no-op beyond debug logging.
 * @return @c kStOK always.
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_sls_Maker::PrintInfo()
 * @brief Prints maker information when debug mode is active.
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_sls_Maker::Clear(const char *opt)
 * @brief Event-level reset; delegates to StMaker::Clear().
 * @param opt Options string forwarded to the base-class implementation.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::readPointFromTable(St_g2t_ssd_hit *g2t_ssd_hit)
 * @brief Load GEANT SSD hits into the StSsdBarrel wafer hit lists (simple path).
 * @details Iterates over all rows of the @c g2t_ssd_hit table.  For each hit
 *          with a valid SSD volume ID (> @c mSsdLayer×1000) the ladder and wafer
 *          indices are decoded and the hit is inserted into the corresponding
 *          StSsdWafer via @c addHit().  No geometry correction is applied.
 * @param g2t_ssd_hit Pointer to the GEANT SSD hit table.
 * @return Number of SSD hits successfully inserted.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::readPointFromTable(St_g2t_svt_hit *g2t_svt_hit)
 * @brief Overload for the legacy SVT hit table; casts and delegates to the SSD overload.
 * @param g2t_svt_hit Pointer to the GEANT SVT hit table (recast as SSD table).
 * @return Number of hits inserted (see SSD overload).
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::removeInactiveHitInTable(St_g2t_ssd_hit *g2t_ssd_hit)
 * @brief Remove hits that fall in detector dead zones from the GEANT table.
 * @details Retrieves the list of inactive (dead-zone) hits from
 *          @c StSsdBarrel::getInactiveHitList() and, exploiting the fact that the
 *          table is often sorted by hit ID, compacts the table in-place by
 *          overwriting removed rows with the next valid row.  After removal
 *          @c StSsdBarrel::renumHitAfterRemove() is called to renumber the
 *          remaining hits.
 * @param g2t_ssd_hit Pointer to the GEANT SSD hit table (modified in place).
 * @return Number of hits removed.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::removeInactiveHitInTable(St_g2t_svt_hit *g2t_svt_hit)
 * @brief Overload for the legacy SVT hit table.
 * @param g2t_svt_hit Pointer to the GEANT SVT hit table (recast as SSD table).
 * @return Number of hits removed (see SSD overload).
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_sls_Maker::chargeSharingOverStrip(slsCtrl_st *ctrl)
 * @brief Trigger the full charge-sharing calculation on all wafers.
 * @details Delegates to @c StSsdBarrel::convertToStrip() passing the complete
 *          set of physics parameters from the @c slsCtrl database struct:
 *          - @c pairCreationEnergy: mean e–h pair creation energy [eV].
 *          - @c nstripInACluster: maximum strip cluster width considered.
 *          - @c parDiffP / @c parDiffN: diffusion spread parameters for the
 *            P-side and N-side respectively.
 *          - @c parIndRightP/N, @c parIndLeftP/N: right- and left-neighbour
 *            capacitive induction amplitudes for each side.
 * @param ctrl Pointer to the first element of the @c slsCtrl table row.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::writeStripToTable(St_sls_strip *sls_strip)
 * @brief Serialise the computed strip signals into the @c sls_strip ROOT table.
 * @details Iterates over every ladder and wafer in StSsdBarrel.  For each wafer
 *          both the P-side and N-side strip lists are traversed; each fired strip
 *          becomes one row in the output table with the following fields:
 *          - @c id: sequential record number (1-based).
 *          - @c adc_count: digitised signal (integer ADC counts).
 *          - @c noise_count: set to 0 at this stage (noise added in St_spa_Maker).
 *          - @c id_strip: packed strip identifier (strip#, side, idWafer).
 *          - @c de: analogue energy-equivalent signal [GeV].
 *          - @c N_hits: number of GEANT hits contributing to the strip.
 *          - @c id_hit[5], @c id_mchit[5], @c id_mctrack[5]: MC truth indices
 *            for up to five contributing hits.
 * @param sls_strip Output table; must already be allocated.
 * @return Total number of strip records written (sum of P-side and N-side).
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::readPointFromTableWithEmbedding(St_g2t_ssd_hit *g2t_ssd_hit, St_g2t_track *g2t_track, Int_t N, ssdWafersPosition_st *positions)
 * @brief Load GEANT hits with full ideal→real geometry correction (embedding path).
 * @details This is the primary hit-loading method used in production.
 *          For each hit in @c g2t_ssd_hit:
 *          -# The track helix is reconstructed from the GEANT momentum vector,
 *             position, particle charge, and the measured magnetic field.
 *          -# ideal2RealTranslation() propagates the helix onto the real wafer
 *             plane (from @c ssdWafersPosition) and updates the hit position and
 *             momentum.
 *          -# The hit is added to the barrel with the corrected position.
 *          -# An @c StMcSsdHit object is created and inserted into the
 *             @c StMcEvent SSD hit collection for downstream truth association.
 *          Hits for which no valid real-geometry wafer intersection is found are
 *          flagged with negative @c de and skipped (not inserted into the barrel).
 * @param g2t_ssd_hit  Pointer to the GEANT SSD hit table.
 * @param g2t_track    Pointer to the GEANT track table (provides particle charge).
 * @param N            Number of rows in the wafer-position table.
 * @param positions    Array of @c ssdWafersPosition_st structs (survey positions).
 * @return Number of hits for which a valid real-geometry wafer was found.
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_sls_Maker::setSsdParameters(ssdDimensions_st *geom_par)
 * @brief Populate internal geometry cache from the @c ssdDimensions table.
 * @details Sets `mSsdLayer=7`, `mNLadder=20`, and reads
 *          `waferHalfActLength`, `waferHalfActWidth`, `wafersPerLadder`,
 *          `stripPerSide`, `stripPitch`, and `stereoAngle` from the first
 *          row of @p geom_par.
 * @param geom_par Pointer to the first element of the @c ssdDimensions table row.
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_sls_Maker::printSsdParameters()
 * @brief Log the cached geometry parameters at INFO level.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::idWaferToWaferNumb(Int_t idWafer)
 * @brief Convert a packed wafer ID to a flat wafer index within the barrel.
 * @details
 * @f[
 *   \text{waferNumb} = (\text{ladder}-1) \times \text{mNWaferPerLadder} + (\text{wafer}-1)
 * @f]
 * where ladder and wafer are extracted from @p idWafer.
 * @param idWafer Packed wafer identifier (@c layer×1000 + wafer×100 + ladder).
 * @return Zero-based flat wafer index in the range @f$[0,\, N_\text{ladders} \times N_\text{wafers/ladder})@f$.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::idWaferToLadderNumb(Int_t idWafer)
 * @brief Extract the zero-based ladder index from a packed wafer ID.
 * @param idWafer Packed wafer identifier.
 * @return Zero-based ladder index in the range @f$[0, 19]@f$.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::waferNumbToIdWafer(Int_t waferNumb)
 * @brief Inverse of idWaferToWaferNumb: convert flat index to packed wafer ID.
 * @param waferNumb Zero-based flat wafer index.
 * @return Packed wafer identifier (@c mSsdLayer×1000 + wafer×100 + ladder).
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::idWaferToWafer(Int_t idWafer)
 * @brief Extract the zero-based wafer-within-ladder index from a packed wafer ID.
 * @details Inline convenience function: @c (idWafer - 7000)/100 - 1.
 * @param idWafer Packed wafer identifier.
 * @return Zero-based wafer index within its ladder.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_sls_Maker::ideal2RealTranslation(StThreeVector<double> *pos, StThreeVector<double> *mtm, double charge, int wafId, int index, ssdWafersPosition_st *positions, Int_t *IL, Int_t *IW)
 * @brief Propagate a track helix from the ideal-geometry hit position to the real wafer plane.
 * @details
 * Algorithm:
 * -# Build an @c StPhysicalHelixD from @p mtm, @p pos, @c mBField, and @p charge.
 * -# Compute the path length @f$s@f$ to the plane defined by the wafer's
 *    survey centre and normal vector (@c pathLength(centre, normal)).
 * -# Evaluate the helix position at @f$s@f$ to obtain the corrected global
 *    hit coordinates; update @p pos in place.
 * -# Transform to the local wafer frame via @c MasterToLocal().
 * -# If the local coordinates are within the active area (IsOnWafer()), record
 *    the corrected ladder/wafer indices in @p IL and @p IW and return @c kStOK.
 * -# Otherwise, loop over the same and the ±1 neighbouring ladders, testing all
 *    their wafers.  If a valid landing wafer is found, return @c kStOk.
 * -# If no valid wafer is found, return @c kStSkip.
 * @param[in,out] pos    Global hit position [cm]; updated to the real-geometry intersection.
 * @param[in,out] mtm    Track momentum [GeV/c]; updated to the momentum at the intersection.
 * @param         charge Particle charge in units of the elementary charge (e.g. +1 or −1).
 * @param         wafId  Original packed wafer ID (ideal geometry).
 * @param         index  Row index of @p wafId in the @p positions array.
 * @param         positions Array of survey-corrected wafer position structs.
 * @param[out]    IL     Zero-based index of the real ladder on which the hit lands.
 * @param[out]    IW     Zero-based index of the real wafer on which the hit lands.
 * @return @c kStOK if a valid real-geometry wafer was found and the intersection
 *         was within the active area; @c kStSkip otherwise.
 */

/**
 * @fn int St_sls_Maker::IsOnWafer(const StThreeVector<double>& LocalPosition)
 * @brief Test whether a local-frame position lies within the active wafer area.
 * @details The active area is a rectangle centred on the origin with full extent
 *          @c mDetectorLargeEdge × @c mDetectorSmallEdge [cm].
 * @param LocalPosition 3-vector in the wafer local coordinate frame [cm].
 * @return 1 if the position is inside the active area; 0 otherwise.
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_sls_Maker::debugUnPeu()
 * @brief Dump debug information for all wafers in all ladders.
 * @details Delegates to @c StSsdBarrel::debugUnPeu() for each (ladder, wafer) pair.
 *          Intended for development use only.
 */


// ============================================================
// Class: St_spa_Maker
// ============================================================

/**
 * @class St_spa_Maker
 * @ingroup StSsdSimulationMaker
 * @brief Strip Pedestal Annihilator — electronics and DAQ simulation for the SSD.
 *
 * @details
 * St_spa_Maker is the second stage of the SSD slow simulation.  It reads the
 * analogue strip signals produced by St_sls_Maker from the @c sls_strip table,
 * adds per-strip Gaussian electronic noise sampled from the @c ssdStripCalib
 * calibration database, applies pedestal subtraction and a DAQ zero-suppression
 * threshold, and writes the surviving strips to the @c spa_strip table.
 *
 * There are 491 520 strips in total (20 ladders, varying wafers/ladder,
 * 768 strips/side × 2 sides).  Each strip receives an independent noise
 * contribution; only strips with a net signal above the DAQ cut appear in the
 * output table.
 *
 * All threshold and noise parameters are read once per run from the
 * @c Calibrations/ssd/ssdStripCalib database path via @c InitRun().
 *
 * ### Data member summary
 *
 * | Member        | Type                   | Description                                          |
 * |---------------|------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
 * | `m_noise`     | `St_ssdStripCalib *`   | Per-strip noise and pedestal calibration table       |
 * | `m_condition` | `St_sdm_condition_db *`| DAQ operating-condition table (zero-suppression cut) |
 * | `m_ctrl`      | `slsCtrl_st *`         | Simulation control parameters (DAQ cut multiplier)  |
 *
 * @authors B. Hippolyte, W. Pinganaud
 * @date 2000
 */

/**
 * @fn St_spa_Maker::St_spa_Maker(const char *name)
 * @brief Constructor. Initialises all data-member pointers to @c nullptr.
 * @param name Maker name; default is @c "spa_strip".
 */

/**
 * @fn St_spa_Maker::~St_spa_Maker()
 * @brief Destructor. No heap memory is owned.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_spa_Maker::Init()
 * @brief One-time initialisation.
 * @details Retrieves the @c sdm_condition_db table from the @c svt/ssd input
 *          database and caches it in @c m_condition.
 * @return Return value of @c StMaker::Init().
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_spa_Maker::InitRun(Int_t runumber)
 * @brief Per-run database retrieval.
 * @details Loads the @c ssdStripCalib table from
 *          @c Calibrations/ssd/ssdStripCalib and the @c slsCtrl table from
 *          StSsdDbMaker.  Returns @c kStFATAL if the noise table is absent.
 * @param runumber STAR run number.
 * @return @c kStOK on success; @c kStFATAL if @c ssdStripCalib is unavailable.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_spa_Maker::Make()
 * @brief Per-event processing — noise injection and DAQ simulation.
 * @details
 * Execution sequence:
 * -# Retrieve the @c sls_strip input table from the data set.
 * -# Create an output @c spa_strip table (capacity 40 000 rows).
 * -# Load the StSsdBarrel instance and call @c readStripFromTable().
 * -# Call @c readNoiseFromTable() to populate per-strip σ and pedestal values.
 * -# Call @c readConditionDbFromTable() for the DAQ operating conditions.
 * -# Call @c addNoiseToStrip() to add Gaussian noise to every fired strip.
 * -# Call @c doDaqSimulation() to apply pedestal subtraction and threshold cut.
 * -# Call @c writeStripToTable() to serialise surviving strips to @c spa_strip.
 * -# Reset the barrel.
 * @return @c kStOK if at least one strip survives; @c kStWarn otherwise.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t St_spa_Maker::Finish()
 * @brief End-of-job clean-up. No-op beyond optional debug logging.
 * @return @c kStOK always.
 */

/**
 * @fn void St_spa_Maker::PrintInfo()
 * @brief Print maker information when debug mode is active.
 */


// ============================================================
// Class: StSsdEmbeddingMaker
// ============================================================

/**
 * @class StSsdEmbeddingMaker
 * @ingroup StSsdSimulationMaker
 * @brief Merges simulated SSD strip signals with real collision data.
 *
 * @details
 * StSsdEmbeddingMaker is the optional third stage of the SSD simulation chain,
 * used when simulated tracks are to be embedded into real STAR collision events.
 * It reads two @c spa_strip tables — one from the SSD simulation (labelled
 * @c SsdSimuData) and one decoded from the real DAQ stream (labelled
 * @c SsdRealData) — and produces a merged @c spa_strip table.
 *
 * ### Merge algorithm
 * For each strip in the real-data table the simulation table is searched for a
 * matching entry (same strip number, wafer ID, and side).
 * - **Match found**: the ADC counts are summed; MC truth fields
 *   (@c id_mchit, @c id_mctrack) from the simulated strip are preserved.
 * - **Real only**: the real strip is copied with zero MC truth.
 * - **Simu only**: the simulated strip is appended with its MC truth intact.
 *
 * ### Operating modes
 * The maker supports three modes, selected via setter methods:
 *
 * | `mDoEmbedding` | `mPlainSimIfNoSSD` | SSD in DAQ? | Behaviour                              |
 * |:--------------:|:------------------:|:-----------:|----------------------------------------|
 * | true (default) | false (default)    | yes         | Full embedding (merge simu + real)     |
 * | true           | false              | no          | Skip event                             |
 * | true           | true               | no          | Plain simulation (simu only)           |
 * | false          | any                | any         | Plain simulation                       |
 *
 * ### Data member summary
 *
 * | Member               | Type             | Description                                           |
 * |----------------------|------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
 * | `m_dimensions`       | `St_ssdDimensions *` | Geometry table (not owned)                       |
 * | `MODE`               | `Int_t`          | Active run mode: 1 = embedding                        |
 * | `mDoEmbedding`       | `Bool_t`         | Enable embedding (default: @c kTRUE)                  |
 * | `mPlainSimIfNoSSD`   | `Bool_t`         | Fall back to plain simulation if no SSD in DAQ        |
 * | `mRunningEmbedding`  | `Bool_t`         | Runtime flag: embedding actually active this event    |
 * | `mSsdLayer`          | `Int_t`          | SSD layer number (7)                                  |
 * | `mNLadder`           | `Int_t`          | Number of ladders (20)                                |
 * | `mNWaferPerLadder`   | `Int_t`          | Number of wafers per ladder (from DB)                 |
 * | `mNStripPerSide`     | `Int_t`          | Number of strips per side per wafer (from DB)         |
 * | `mDetectorLargeEdge` | `Float_t`        | Full active length along beam [cm]                    |
 * | `mDetectorSmallEdge` | `Float_t`        | Full active width (transverse) [cm]                   |
 * | `mStripPitch`        | `Float_t`        | Strip pitch [cm]                                      |
 * | `mTheta`             | `Float_t`        | Stereo angle [rad]                                    |
 * | `mSsdSimuData`       | `St_spa_strip *` | Input: simulated strips (not owned)                   |
 * | `mSsdrealData`       | `St_spa_strip *` | Input: real DAQ strips (not owned)                    |
 * | `mSsdSimuReal`       | `St_spa_strip *` | Output: merged strip table (owned)                    |
 * | `mDimensions`        | `ssdDimensions_st *` | Cached pointer to raw geometry struct             |
 * | `mCurrentEvent`      | `StEvent *` (prot.) | Pointer to the reconstructed event                 |
 * | `hStripsSimu`        | `TH1F *` (prot.)  | Diagnostic: log10(# simu strips after DAQ cut)       |
 * | `hStripsReal`        | `TH1F *` (prot.)  | Diagnostic: log10(# real strips after DAQ cut)       |
 * | `hStripsCommon`      | `TH1F *` (prot.)  | Diagnostic: # strips common to simu and real          |
 * | `myfile`             | `TFile *` (prot.) | Optional output file for diagnostics                  |
 *
 * @author J. Bouchet
 * @date 2008
 */

/**
 * @fn StSsdEmbeddingMaker::StSsdEmbeddingMaker(const char *name)
 * @brief Constructor. Sets embedding mode as default; clears strip table pointers.
 * @details Sets @c mDoEmbedding = @c kTRUE, @c mPlainSimIfNoSSD = @c kFALSE,
 *          and initialises @c mSsdrealData and @c mSsdSimuData to @c nullptr.
 * @param name Maker name; default is @c "SsdEmbed".
 */

/**
 * @fn StSsdEmbeddingMaker::~StSsdEmbeddingMaker()
 * @brief Destructor. No heap memory is owned.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::Init()
 * @brief One-time initialisation.
 * @details If the @c ".histos" attribute is set, allocates the three diagnostic
 *          histograms (@c hStripsSimu, @c hStripsReal, @c hStripsCommon).
 * @return Return value of @c StMaker::Init().
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::InitRun(int RunNo)
 * @brief Per-run database retrieval.
 * @details Verifies that an @c StSsdBarrel instance exists, then loads the
 *          @c ssdDimensions table from @c Geometry/ssd and calls
 *          setSsdParameters().
 * @param RunNo STAR run number.
 * @return @c kStOk on success; @c kStFatal if the geometry database is unavailable.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::Make()
 * @brief Per-event processing — embedding decision and merge.
 * @details
 * -# Decides whether embedding can actually run:
 *    if @c mDoEmbedding is true, calls NoSsd() to check DAQ stream.
 * -# Calls GetSsdData() to retrieve the simu and real strip tables.
 * -# If running in embedding mode (MODE=1) calls AddRawData() to perform the merge.
 * -# Fills diagnostic histograms if @c ".histos" is set.
 * @return @c kStOk on success; propagates error codes from GetSsdData().
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::Finish()
 * @brief End-of-job clean-up.
 * @return @c kStOK always.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::GetSsdData()
 * @brief Retrieve simulated and real @c spa_strip tables from the data set.
 * @details Looks for the @c SsdSimuData dataset (simulated strips) and the
 *          @c SsdRealData dataset (real strips).  Returns an error if either
 *          table is absent or empty.
 * @return @c kStOk if both tables are found and non-empty;
 *         @c kStErr if either table is missing or empty.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::AddRawData()
 * @brief Perform the three-way merge of simulated and real strip tables.
 * @details
 * Creates the output @c spa_strip table @c mSsdSimuReal (capacity 50 000 rows).
 * Three passes:
 * -# **Common strips**: for each real strip, search the simulation table for a
 *    strip with the same (strip#, wafer, side); if found, sum the ADC counts and
 *    write the entry, keeping MC truth from the simulated strip.  Track the
 *    matched strip IDs in @c IdCommon[].
 * -# **Real-only strips**: real strips with no simulation counterpart are copied
 *    with zero MC truth fields.
 * -# **Simu-only strips**: simulated strips not listed in @c IdCommon are appended
 *    with their own MC truth fields.
 * @return Total number of strip records in the merged output table.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::NoSsd()
 * @brief Check whether SSD data are present in the current DAQ event.
 * @details Retrieves @c StDAQReader from the chain and calls
 *          @c StDAQReader::SSDPresent().
 * @return @c kTRUE if no SSD data are found in the DAQ stream (or if the
 *         DAQ reader is unavailable); @c kFALSE if SSD data are present.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StSsdEmbeddingMaker::CheckTables()
 * @brief Dump the contents of the simulated (and optionally real) strip tables.
 * @details Decodes each strip's geometry (ladder, wafer, side, strip number) and
 *          logs it at DEBUG level.  Called only when @c Debug() is true.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StSsdEmbeddingMaker::setDoEmbedding(Bool_t doIt)
 * @brief Enable or disable embedding mode.
 * @param doIt @c kTRUE to attempt embedding; @c kFALSE to run plain simulation.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StSsdEmbeddingMaker::setPlainSimEvenIfNoSSD(Bool_t doIt)
 * @brief Control fallback behaviour when no SSD data exist in the DAQ stream.
 * @param doIt @c kTRUE to run plain simulation if no SSD is found in DAQ;
 *             @c kFALSE (default) to skip the event entirely in that case.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StSsdEmbeddingMaker::idWaferToWafer(Int_t idWafer)
 * @brief Extract the zero-based wafer-within-ladder index from a packed wafer ID.
 * @details Inline: @c (idWafer - 7000)/100 - 1.
 * @param idWafer Packed wafer identifier.
 * @return Zero-based wafer index within its ladder.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StSsdEmbeddingMaker::setSsdParameters(ssdDimensions_st *geom_par)
 * @brief Populate internal geometry cache from the @c ssdDimensions table.
 * @details Sets `mSsdLayer=7`, `mNLadder=20`, and reads geometry fields from
 *          the first row of @p geom_par.  Identical logic to
 *          St_sls_Maker::setSsdParameters().
 * @param geom_par Pointer to the first element of the @c ssdDimensions table row.
 */
